The rule: any complete row or column of a single color (the "line" color) has those cells recolored to 2; everything else stays.

```python
def transform(grid):
    R, C = len(grid), len(grid[0])
    out = [row[:] for row in grid]
    for i in range(R):
        if all(grid[i][j] == grid[i][0] for j in range(C)):
            out[i] = [2] * C
    for j in range(C):
        if all(grid[i][j] == grid[0][j] for i in range(R)):
            for i in range(R):
                out[i][j] = 2
    return out
```

